.TH FAMILY 1
.SH NAME
family \- write the part source of a member of a family of the library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B family screws
.I size style length
.br
.B family packages
.I name
.br
.B family inserts
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Family
writes on the standard output the source
.RI ( part (5))
of a plain exact solid, named body, for a row of a table of the library
.RI ( plicad-lib (7)):
.TP 10
.B screws
a head and a shank of the size and style, the shank
.I length
long down from z = 0; a flat head is a cone of its angle down from
z = 0, flush there, the others a cylinder up from z = 0;
.TP
.B packages
a box of the length along x and the width, centered on the z axis,
its height up from z = 0;
.TP
.B inserts
the body of the hardware, a cylinder up from z = 0.
.PP
A table of the name in the current directory adds its rows to those of
the library, before them: a row it lacks comes from the library.
.SH EXAMPLES
family screws M3 pan 10 | extrude \- | bool \- >screw.st
.br
family packages soic\-8 | extrude \- >soic8.st
.SH SEE ALSO
plicad-lib(7), part(5), extrude(1), place(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A row that the table lacks, or that is short, is refused.
